            <HeadlineEnglish>The official Sample Ballot for the November 3 General Election is now available</HeadlineEnglish>
            <SubtitleEnglish>Will be available in print in several Miami-Dade newspapers in the coming days and
               at government offices, libraries, Supervisor of Elections locations, during early
               voting at all sites, on Election Day, and at other key distribution points</SubtitleEnglish>
            <DescriptionEnglish>Miami-Dade County Supervisor of Elections Alina Garcia is encouraging voters to make
               a plan for the November 3 General Election beginning with reviewing the official Sample
               Ballot now available on our website.</DescriptionEnglish>
            <PressReleaseBodyEnglish>&lt;p&gt;Miami-Dade County Supervisor of Elections Alina Garcia is encouraging voters to
               make a plan for the November 3 General &amp;nbsp;Election beginning with reviewing the
               official Sample Ballot now available at &lt;a href="https://www.miamidade.gov/elections/library/2026-11-03-general-election-sample-ballot.pdf"&gt;https://www.miamidade.gov/elections/library/2026-11-03-general-election-sample-ballot.pdf&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
               &lt;p&gt;The official Sample Ballot allows voters to study the contests, candidates, and
               questions that will appear on the ballot before heading to the polls or completing
               their Vote-by-Mail ballot. Reviewing a Sample Ballot in advance helps voters make
               informed decisions and ensures a quicker, smoother, and more efficient voting experience.
               Voters can also view their customized personal ballots at &lt;a href="https://www.votemiamidade.gov/elections/voters/information.page"&gt;https://www.votemiamidade.gov/elections/voters/information.page&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
               &lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;Our goal is to make voting as easy and accessible as possible for every
               voter in Miami-Dade County,&amp;rdquo; said &lt;strong&gt;Supervisor Garcia&lt;/strong&gt;. &amp;ldquo;By
               reviewing the Sample Ballot and especially your customized personal ballot before
               voting, you can feel prepared, confident, and ready to make your voice heard.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;
               &lt;p&gt;Voters are encouraged to visit &lt;strong&gt;votemiamidade.gov&lt;/strong&gt; to view important
               election information, including voting locations, deadlines, and other voter resources.
               The 2026 General Election Master Ballot with all contests and questions can be viewed
               at &lt;a href="https://www.miamidade.gov/elections/library/2026-11-03-general-election-master-ballot.pdf"&gt;https://www.miamidade.gov/elections/library/2026-11-03-general-election-master-ballot.pdf&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
               &lt;p&gt;For more information, please call &lt;strong&gt;305-499-VOTE (8683)&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</PressReleaseBodyEnglish>
