   <h2 class="press__subTitle general-page__subTitle">Will be available in print in several Miami-Dade newspapers in the coming days and
      at government offices, libraries, Supervisor of Elections locations, during early
      voting at all sites, on Election Day, and at other key distribution points</h2>
   <div class="press__description normal-bullets"><strong>MIAMI-DADE ( September 22, 2026 )– </strong><p>Miami-Dade County Supervisor of Elections Alina Garcia is encouraging voters to make a plan for the November 3 General &nbsp;Election beginning with reviewing the official Sample Ballot now available at <a href="https://www.miamidade.gov/elections/library/2026-11-03-general-election-sample-ballot.pdf">https://www.miamidade.gov/elections/library/2026-11-03-general-election-sample-ballot.pdf</a>.</p>
<p>The official Sample Ballot allows voters to study the contests, candidates, and questions that will appear on the ballot before heading to the polls or completing their Vote-by-Mail ballot. Reviewing a Sample Ballot in advance helps voters make informed decisions and ensures a quicker, smoother, and more efficient voting experience. Voters can also view their customized personal ballots at <a href="https://www.votemiamidade.gov/elections/voters/information.page">https://www.votemiamidade.gov/elections/voters/information.page</a>.</p>
<p>&ldquo;Our goal is to make voting as easy and accessible as possible for every voter in Miami-Dade County,&rdquo; said <strong>Supervisor Garcia</strong>. &ldquo;By reviewing the Sample Ballot and especially your customized personal ballot before voting, you can feel prepared, confident, and ready to make your voice heard.&rdquo;</p>
<p>Voters are encouraged to visit <strong>votemiamidade.gov</strong> to view important election information, including voting locations, deadlines, and other voter resources. The 2026 General Election Master Ballot with all contests and questions can be viewed at <a href="https://www.miamidade.gov/elections/library/2026-11-03-general-election-master-ballot.pdf">https://www.miamidade.gov/elections/library/2026-11-03-general-election-master-ballot.pdf</a>.</p>
<p>For more information, please call <strong>305-499-VOTE (8683)</strong>.</p></div>
   <div class="col s12"></div>
   <div class="release__footer">
      <p><b># # #</b></p>
      <p class="press__footer-ada">To request materials in accessible format, sign language interpreters, and/or any
         accommodation to participate in any County-sponsored program or meeting, please contact
         the <a href="https://www.miamidade.gov/global/ada-coordinators.page">ADA Coordinator</a>, five days in advance to initiate your request. TTY users may also call 711 (Florida
         Relay Service).</p>
      <p class="release__footer-name">Alina Garcia, Miami-Dade Supervisor of Elections</p>
      <p><strong>Miami-Dade Supervisor of Elections</strong><br>2700 NW 87 Avenue, 
          Miami, FL  33172</p>
